@@ -34,6 +34,8 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 - `codebase_reference_checklist` is a field of the `validate_task_spec` envelope and of the `validate_plan` response, no longer a finding. `validate_task_spec` returns one entry per claim the reviewer could not verify; `validate_plan` one entry per affected task. It does not count as a finding, as a minor on the verdict ladder, or toward `noise_cluster`, so three unverifiable references no longer lift a clean spec to `warn`. The summary block prints it under `checklist:`, `next_action` names it, and `events.jsonl` records its length as `checklist_items`. A caller that read the checklist from `findings` / `plan_findings` by its `codebase_reference_checklist` criterion must read the new field.
 - A path a task lists in its own `**Files:**` section is not a codebase claim. `validate_plan` drops an `unverifiable_codebase_claim` whose evidence names only such paths (line anchors included) before building `codebase_reference_checklist`, and its prompt tells the reviewer not to raise one. `validate_task_spec` does the same for the paths a `**Files:**` section in `context` lists and for the paths the named plan run recorded for the task. A claim that also names a symbol, another path or a convention stays on the checklist. The plan run keeps those paths in memory only; no stats file or ledger line carries them.
 - The `PostToolUse` hook `examples/hooks/codescene-log.sh` is retired: the server writes the same file, and with both in place a run would be counted twice. The script now writes nothing and exits 0, so a `settings.json` that still registers it does not fail; remove the entry. `docs/team-setup/codescene-stats.md` describes the server-written channel and what differs from the hook's records.
+- A `validate_task_spec` call that passes no `plan_run_id` is attached by title when the server holds exactly one live plan run and `task_title` matches exactly one of that run's plan headings: the task gets its `plan_run_report` row and a minor `plan_run_id` finding names the run. With two live runs, or a title that matches no heading or several, nothing is attached and the earlier advisory is returned. Together with `validate_plan` rounds keeping one run per plan, this closes the gap in which tasks were validated but never counted.
+- The controller protocol (§5.1) tells the controller to pass the previous round's `plan_run_id` when it calls `validate_plan` again.
 
