+**Rounds (v0.27.0+).** `validate_plan` accepts `plan_run_id`, the id an earlier round returned. A task is unchanged when its heading and body are byte-identical to the earlier round's; unchanged tasks keep their results and are not sent to the reviewer. The plan-level pass runs again only when the plan text changed, and is shown the earlier plan-level findings so it drops what the edit resolved and keeps the id of what still holds. `controller_rulings` and `controller_verified_references` are applied to carried results as well, so adding a ruling costs no reviewer call. Changing `project_knowledge`, `mode`, the model or the attached files reviews every task again under the same id. An unknown or expired id falls back to a full review under a new run, with a minor `plan_run_id` finding; omit the argument to force a full review. Callers that pass no id keep the three-minute pass cache.
 
